.TH tapectl-location-add 1  "tapectl-location-add " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-location\-add \- Add a storage location
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl location add\fR [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-kind\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a storage location
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Description. For a warehouse this is where the endpoint or prefix goes (e.g. "s3://bucket/prefix") \-\- there is deliberately no separate URI column (issue #73)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR [default: shelf]
Kind of location (ADR\-0006). A `shelf` holds physical cartridges; a `warehouse` is cold cloud storage that can only receive recorded deposits (`volume deposit add`)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
shelf
.IP \(bu 2
warehouse
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Location name (e.g., "home\-rack", "parents\-house")
